        "title": "French - Language Reference",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "VOWELS — French has ~15 vowel phonemes (English has ~12-14)\n  Key distinctions English lacks:\n  [y]  — \"u\" sound: pur, lune, tu (round your lips as for \"oo\", say \"ee\")\n  [ø]  — \"eu\" sound: feu, peur, bleu (round lips for \"o\", say \"e\")\n  [œ]  — \"eu\" open: peur, cœur, fleur\n  Nasals: an/en [ɑ̃], in/ain [ɛ̃], on [ɔ̃], un [œ̃] (merging with in)"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-FRENCH.md#011",
      "path": [
        "04-FRENCH.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:world-languages:04-french, git-history:world-languages:04-french]",
